-- title:
--   Non-ordinary residual points: p∤ M and aₚ a non-unit
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$, i.e. a $k$-vector space $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho\colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$, and $N\geq 1$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2\nmid N$, such that the integral lattice of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ spans over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$, to $k$, and assume $\theta$ computes Frobenius characteristic polynomials of $\bar\rho$: for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (lying in the decomposition subgroup and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$), $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Assume $\bar\rho$, viewed as an adic representation over the local ring $k$, is not ordinary at $p$: for some valuation subring $P$ over $p$ there is no $k$-line $L=k\cdot b_0$ spanned by a member of a basis of $V$ which is stable under the decomposition subgroup at $P$ and satisfies $\sigma v-v\in L$ for all $v\in V$ and all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a second such complete discrete valuation ring, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module along a local structure map, and $\psi$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to $\mathcal O'$. Finally let $M\mid N$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose good eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M$), let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra of level $M$ away from $S\setminus\{p\}$ to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S\setminus\{p\}$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$ such that for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ the value $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ agrees with $\psi$ applied to the image of $T_\ell$ in the localised Hecke algebra. Then $p\nmid M$, and (for any such proof of $p\nmid M$, which makes $T_p$ available at level $M$ away from $S\setminus\{p\}$) the element $\iota(\chi_g(T_p))$ is not a unit of $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   This is the local input at $p$ for points of the localised anemic Hecke algebra attached to a residual representation that is not ordinary at $p$: the newform behind such a point has level prime to $p$ and is supersingular at $p$, so that both roots of $X^2-a_pX+p$ reduce to zero. It is used in the computation of the multiplicity of such a point in the residual fibre, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.sum_rootMultiplicity_residual_eq_two_of_not_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.sum_rootMultiplicity_residual_eq_two_of_not_isOrdinaryAt).
